        "summary": "Fixed. Only `electron/tool-output.js` changed; `node public.cjs .` passes.\n\nTwo defects repaired:\n- `capture` stored only `text.slice(0, limit)`, dropping characters beyond the limit and corrupting eviction accounting (`bytes` added full length but subtracted the truncated length). Now stores the full string, so every character is retrievable and `bytes` stays consistent.\n- `read` sliced `text.slice(start+1, start+count+1)` \u2014 an off-by-one that skipped the first character and duplicated/lost others. Now slices `text.slice(start, end)` with `end = min(start+count, length)`, and the metadata range and `next offset=${end}` exactly agree with the returned page, clamping offset to the output length.\n\nVerified: full round-trip paging reconstructs the raw string with no skip/duplication, partial final page marks `; end]` and omits `next offset`, limits default to 12000/clamp to 24000/min 1, previews stay bounded, short outputs return unchanged, and eviction holds the 8 MB bound with `bytes` matching stored lengths.",
